e's young xteeam .wa3 blighted."}, {"id": "p4b84", "x": 20.992, "y": 54.674, "w": 11.889, "h": 4.45, "text": "We know oif several eases where pil\ngrims have come to Dakota with little\nor iio summer clothing, thinking that\nit wonld'be'tiseless here. The pores of\nourek'ji fairly wept at their delusion\nTuesday, when we saw the thermometer\nregister lOt in the shade and never\ncracKasmile."}, {"id": "p4b85", "x": 21.037, "y": 59.283, "w": 11.781, "h": 8.85, "text": "Warren Pwkard, of Warren, Oli'o one\not the most prominent iron and lumber\nmen in. that state and J. J. Fisher, a\nwealthy young business man of Allen\ntown, Pa^ spent the first of the week in\nMedora and vicinity. They expressed\nthemselves as greatly pleased with their\nvisit, especially at their treatment at\nthe beef camp on .Davis creek. As near\nas they could,.make out, everything was\ndone according to Hoyle, except that\nthey looked in,Vain for the plaao to ac\ncompany the eyenihg lullaby of the cow\nboys when they were singing the herd to\nsleep, after liaving been driven up to the\ncorrall to be milked."}, {"id": "p4b86", "x": 21.048, "y": 68.292, "w": 11.769, "h": 12.759, "text": "We neglected. ifi our last issne to men\ntion the Bad Lands minstrel entertain\nment, given by home talent at the rink,\non the evepinyg .of the fourth of July.\nThe variefy pt^ of the entertainment\nwould have been a complete success, if\njve had biougfit-our guns along and\nkilled all the performers at the begin\nrifiigof ttfe ffifet act'/^fhe, orchestra,led\nby Mose de Spicer was,8impiy indeseri*\nbable. To escape a ponular uprising,\nMose fled the next mprnlng for the Paci\nfic coast. Two other, meihbers of the\ngang, for this or some outer, reason, skip\nto-night for the Big. Horn country. One\nof the fioest pieces of legerdemain ever\nwitnessed was the invisible way in\nwhich ih* invisible Prof. Welling delu\nded a-.confiding public into believing\nthat there Vjas 8 professor on the stage\nwho knew-the. difference between A\nsleight of band trick and four dollars a\nweek.'"}, {"id": "p4b87", "x": 21.02, "y": 81.701, "w": 11.718, "h": 2.355, "text": "'M '*Hotel Arrivals.\nThe following perqpns registered' at\nthe Northern Pacific- during the last\nweek: (i,, P. .Williams, Bismarck"}, {"id": "p4b88", "x": 20.486, "y": 89.524, "w": 0.114, "h": 0.306, "text": "1"}, {"id": "p4b89", "x": 14.624, "y": 90.015, "w": 1.723, "h": 0.536, "text": "Stowe"}, {"id": "p4b90", "x": 6.266, "y": 90.71, "w": 14.288, "h": 1.655, "text": "-L, Parsons calling for any of the above\nplouo fifty\"Wwrtlwi.\"\u2022.-\u2022\nif. F, V\u00abaDriesche, Postmaster."}, {"id": "p4b91", "x": 26.336, "y": 87.92, "w": 6.482, "h": 0.536, "text": "Warren Paclwrd,War-"}, {"id": "p4b92", "x": 20.895, "y": 88.548, "w": 11.985, "h": 3.889, "text": "reny Ohio John J. Fisher, Allentown,^\nPa. Fred-Ailen, Glendire 'James Basch,\nStPanl Dr.H.-W. Coe, Mandan Qeo.\nAuld, Belfield -A. Connell, J. B/^oqa\nghan, Greei Bay, Wis. Gust Noble, Deca\ntur, Ind. J.W.Bnster, Hashknife raaeh\nS.lL Emerton, C. D. Edick, Bismarck."}, {"id": "p4b93", "x": 34.87, "y": 5.51, "w": 7.698, "h": 1.228, "text": "GENERAL"}, {"id": "p4b94", "x": 31.26, "y": 11.657, "w": 1.217, "h": 0.536, "text": "de^s."}, {"id": "p4b95", "x": 24.932, "y": 13.191, "w": 1.694, "h": 0.541, "text": "Jq1t14"}, {"id": "p4b96", "x": 30.151, "y": 13.191, "w": 2.314, "h": 0.541, "text": "11Q deV"}, {"id": "p4b97", "x": 20.685, "y": 13.543, "w": 11.855, "h": 2.56, "text": "At0d'clovkp. m., July ...10T degsv\nLOWSiT TSMfBttftTDBB,\nAt 6 o'clock a. tn July ll, above zero.64 de^s.\nAt lio'cUjo.Viu., Jnlv 10, aIjovo aero 74 doss.\nAt 0 clock p. n\\., Julv 13, above *cro -ti8 degs.\nCoiGvatday.... Jj]ly"}, {"id": "p4b98", "x": 37.111, "y": 13.819, "w": 3.474, "h": 0.541, "text": "\u2014OF THE-"}, {"id": "p4b99", "x": 33.034, "y": 15.705, "w": 11.855, "h": 2.615, "text": "N. P. R. 0. GO,"}, {"id": "p4b100", "x": 31.283, "y": 16.543, "w": 1.325, "h": 0.888, "text": "days.\nda